Currently, when you wish for an artifact, if you don't get it, you
don't get anything.  What if, instead, you received the base item named
for the artifact?  That is, I wish for the blessed Ogresmasher, but too
many artifacts (potentially including Ogresmasher itself) already exist
in game, so I end up with a blessed war hammer named Ogresmasher?

This would make wishing for artifacts slightly harder, since you may
not be able to tell if you got the real deal or not without an ID (or
enlightenment for some artifacts, or seeing a bolt of lightning for
Mjollnir, etc.)  I don't think it's unbalancing, since the base items
(other than tsurugi) are all fairly easy to come by (and relatively
cheap, too).  The only issue I can think of is that Sting and Orcrist
would be obtainable through wishing even on a failed roll, but they're
so easy to get already, I don't think it's a major issue.

Thoughts?
